{"No handling for client_sample_rate == 0 - risk of division by zero when deriving sample_weight as 1/sample_rate": 0.5612425208091736, "Unstable use of Python built-in hash() in cache key - hash() is randomized per interpreter process causing different cache keys across processes and restarts, breaking cache visibility and invalidation": 0.9603740572929382, "No error handling or fallback when upsampled_count() Snuba query fails - no try/except around Snuba query calls to catch failures specific to upsampled_count() aggregates": 0.37564876675605774, "upsampled_count registered only in Discover dataset but applied to errors dataset - will cause runtime UnknownFunction error for queries routed through errors dataset": 0.952574610710144, "Factories.store_event mutates normalized_data by adding 'sample_rate' from contexts.error_sampling - may change event semantics and affect tests relying on sample_rate absence": 0.6896586418151855}